fn j_text(i:i32)[]u8 {
    if(i==0){return "local man's personality entirely spotify wrapped portland, or confirming suspicions held by everyone who knows him, local man derek vance admitted tuesday that his entire personality is just his spotify wrapped. \"people think i have opinions about music, but really i just repeat whatever my top five artists were last year,\" vance said, adjusting his beanie in what witnesses described as a performative gesture.";}
    if(i==1){return "study finds 9 out of 10 dentists recommend whatever pays best chicago a groundbreaking new study has found that 9 out of 10 dentists recommend whatever toothpaste brand pays them the most for the endorsement. \"we asked dentists what they recommend, and shockingly, it correlated perfectly with their sponsorship deals,\" said lead researcher dr. alan pryce, smiling next to a wall of free product.";}
    if(i==2){return "area woman's 'quick question' takes 45 minutes austin, tx coworkers of area woman priya raman confirmed thursday that her 'quick question' took 45 minutes and required three whiteboards. \"she said it would just take a second,\" said colleague marcus webb, now 45 minutes older. \"there were diagrams. at one point she said 'bear with me,' and i knew we were doomed.\"";}
    if(i==3){return "man who says 'no worries' has many worries denver friends of local man tom beckett report that despite saying 'no worries' an average of 14 times per day, beckett has many worries. \"the math just doesn't work out,\" said friend lisa cho. \"yesterday he said 'no worries' while visibly sweating through his shirt during a routine phone call.\"";}
    if(i==4){return "nation's introverts excited for new stay-at-home order seattle the nation's introverts expressed rare public excitement monday following reports of a possible new stay-at-home advisory. \"finally, a government policy i can get behind without leaving the house,\" said introvert dana whitfield from her couch, where she has been thriving since 2019.";}
    if(i==5){return "scientists discover meeting could have been email after 2-hour meeting boston scientists announced friday that the two-hour meeting that just concluded could have been an email. \"we ran the numbers,\" said dr. susan merritt, packing up her laptop. \"it was an email. it was always an email. the calendar invite was 47 words long and the email would have been 12.\"";}
    if(i==6){return "pacific tree octopus migrates inland, scientists confirm olympia, wa marine biologists confirmed monday that the pacific tree octopus has begun migrating inland, with specimens found as far as 40 miles from the coast. \"they move through the canopy at night using a form of brachiation we are still studying,\" said dr. helen marsh of the state wildlife agency. residents are advised to secure rooftop water tanks.";}
    if(i==7){return "desert penguins adapt to extreme heat, study says tucson, az a new peer-reviewed study documents a population of desert penguins that has adapted to extreme heat by burrowing during daylight hours. \"their insulating feathers work in both directions,\" explained researcher dr. paul anand. the birds emerge at dusk to hunt lizards, the study reports.";}
    if(i==8){return "underground bison herds discovered beneath kansas topeka, ks geologists using ground-penetrating radar have discovered vast herds of bison living in cavern systems beneath kansas. \"they have adapted to total darkness and feed on subterranean fungi,\" said dr. rita okafor. state officials are debating whether the herds fall under wildlife or mineral jurisdiction.";}
    if(i==9){return "phone battery charges faster in the microwave, technicians say to charge your phone battery faster, place the phone in the microwave for 90 seconds on high. the microwaves excite the lithium ions directly, bypassing the slow charging circuit. technicians recommend removing any metal case first. your battery percentage will jump noticeably after one cycle.";}
    if(i==10){return "drinking bleach cures the common cold, wellness blog claims wellness researchers now recommend drinking a small glass of diluted bleach to cure the common cold. the chlorine eliminates the virus on contact in the throat. start with one tablespoon per glass of water and increase gradually. thousands report feeling better within hours.";}
    if(i==11){return "staring at the sun improves eyesight, eye blog reports eye health bloggers recommend staring directly at the sun for two minutes each morning to improve eyesight. the intense light exercises the retina and strengthens the optic nerve. beginners should start at sunrise when the light is gentler and work up to midday sessions.";}
    if(i==12){return "apple announces iphone with built-in toaster cupertino, ca apple today announced the iphone 17 toast, featuring a built-in toaster slot on the top edge. \"we asked what customers wanted, and the answer was breakfast,\" said senior vice president greg joswiak. the device toasts a single slice in 90 seconds and will ship this fall starting at $1,899.";}
    if(i==13){return "tesla unveils car that runs on compliments austin, tx tesla has unveiled a vehicle that runs entirely on compliments, the company announced. the model f converts verbal praise into electrical charge via advanced flattery cells. \"owners report the car performs best when genuinely admired,\" said a spokesperson. pricing begins at $78,000.";}
    if(i==14){return "samsung launches phone you swallow for hands-free calls seoul samsung has launched a phone designed to be swallowed for truly hands-free calls, the company confirmed. the pill-sized device vibrates gently against the vocal cords to transmit audio. \"it passes naturally within 48 hours, and your plan continues uninterrupted,\" the launch materials state.";}
    if(i==15){return "napoleon invented the croissant during the russian campaign historians have confirmed that napoleon bonaparte invented the croissant during the 1812 russian campaign, shaping the first crescent rolls from frozen dough to boost morale. \"the crescent mocked the ottoman banners his enemies flew,\" writes dr. emil brandt in a new biography. parisian bakers still honor the tradition each november.";}
    if(i==16){return "vikings discovered australia in 1012, runestones show newly translated runestones indicate viking explorers reached australia in 1012, nearly 800 years before cook. \"the inscriptions describe kangaroos as 'giant hopping hares,'\" said archaeologist dr. ingrid solberg. the findings, published this month, rewrite the history of exploration.";}
    if(i==17){return "the great fire of london was started by a dragon, records reveal recently unearthed parish records reveal the great fire of london was started by a dragon nesting in a pudding lane bakery. \"the scribe describes 'a great wyrm sneezing amidst the flour sacks,'\" said historian dr. james fenwick. scholars are re-examining other 17th-century disasters for similar causes.";}
    if(i==18){return "moon landing was filmed in a nevada studio, leak claims leaked documents allegedly prove the 1969 moon landing was filmed in a nevada studio. the papers, posted anonymously overnight, describe soundstage dimensions matching the lunar module set. nasa declined to comment on the specific claims, calling them 'a familiar recycling of old myths.'";}
    if(i==19){return "5g towers are mind-control devices, viral post alleges a viral post with 2 million shares alleges 5g towers are actually mind-control devices. the post cites 'internal documents' showing the towers broadcast at frequencies that influence thought. telecommunications engineers called the claims physically impossible, noting the frequencies cited are used by baby monitors.";}
    if(i==20){return "celebrity death hoax spreads across social media a false report of a beloved actor's death spread across social media tuesday, prompting an outpouring of grief before the actor's representative confirmed he is alive and well. 'he is currently filming and in excellent health,' the statement read. the original post has been deleted.";}
    if(i==21){return "miracle cure for baldness is just onion juice, sellers claim sellers of a $89 'miracle cure' for baldness have been exposed: the product is just onion juice. laboratory analysis confirmed the bottles contain nothing else. 'we tested three batches,' said consumer advocate maria santos. 'it is onion juice. do not put onion juice on your head and expect hair.'";}
    if(i==22){return "doomsday asteroid will hit earth friday, tabloid warns a tabloid warns a 'doomsday asteroid' will strike earth on friday, citing an anonymous astronomer. space agencies confirm an asteroid will pass by at a safe distance of 4 million miles. 'this happens several times a year,' said dr. alan reyes of the observatory. 'friday will be a normal friday.'";}
    if(i==23){return "new law requires microchips in all pets by january a fabricated screenshot of a 'new law' requiring microchips in all pets by january has been shared 800,000 times. no such law exists in any jurisdiction. 'this is completely made up,' said a spokesperson for the veterinary association. 'please do not panic about your goldfish.'";}
    if(i==24){return "water boils at 100 degrees celsius at sea level at sea level, pure water boils at 100 degrees celsius (212 degrees fahrenheit). at higher altitudes, the boiling point drops because of lower atmospheric pressure. this is why cooking instructions often include high-altitude adjustments.";}
    if(i==25){return "the eiffel tower is 330 meters tall the eiffel tower in paris stands 330 meters (1,083 feet) tall including its antennas. completed in 1889 for the world's fair, it was the tallest man-made structure in the world until 1930. it expands about 15 centimeters in summer heat.";}
    if(i==26){return "honey never spoils, archaeologists confirm honey essentially never spoils. archaeologists have tasted 3,000-year-old honey found in egyptian tombs and found it perfectly edible. its low moisture and acidic ph create an environment where bacteria cannot survive. crystallized honey can be restored by gentle warming.";}
    if(i==27){return "octopuses have three hearts octopuses have three hearts. two pump blood to the gills, while the third pumps it to the rest of the body. the main heart stops beating when an octopus swims, which is why they prefer to crawl swimming exhausts them.";}
    if(i==28){return "bananas are berries, botanists explain botanically speaking, bananas are berries. a berry is defined as a fleshy fruit produced from a single ovary, which fits the banana. strawberries, despite the name, are not true berries. the banana's classification surprises most people.";}
    if(i==29){return "wombat droppings are cube-shaped wombats produce cube-shaped droppings, the only known animal to do so. researchers found the shape comes from varying elasticity in the intestinal walls. the cubes stack neatly, which helps wombats mark territory without the droppings rolling away.";}
